          "normalized_title": "Scientists Discover a Hidden Problem in Decades of Spacecraft Data",
          "normalized_summary": "Different processes can produce similar spacecraft observations, making it difficult to determine how particles move through Earth’s radiation belt. A spacecraft passing through Earth’s radiation belts can record particle behavior that looks random even when the underlying motion is highly organized. New research suggests that the limited resolution of spacecraft measurements can hide fine structures [...]",
