          "normalized_title": "Scientists Discover a Hidden World of Fungi 1,640 Feet Beneath Michigan",
          "normalized_summary": "A hidden ecosystem beneath Michigan contains abundant fungi and other complex life that may affect underground carbon. Far beneath Michigan, water trapped inside ancient rock contains a dense and unexpectedly diverse community of fungi. A University of Michigan study suggests that these organisms are far more abundant in the deep subsurface than scientists once assumed, [...]",
